Chapter: Kinematic
  cites Punctual chapter IntOps

 2D and 3D kinematic primitives safe for real-time contexts. Every
 function is punctual: no heap, no recursion, bounded instruction
 count.

 All operations take individual coordinate components rather than
 aggregate types, keeping them allocation-free. Results that would
 be multi-valued (like cross-3d) are split into per-component
 functions.

 To dot-2d gives the dot product of two 2D vectors.
 To dot-3d gives the dot product of two 3D vectors.
 To cross-2d gives the scalar cross product (z-component of 3D cross)
 of two 2D vectors. Useful for orientation tests.
 To cross-3d-x gives the x-component of the cross product.
 To cross-3d-y gives the y-component of the cross product.
 To cross-3d-z gives the z-component of the cross product.
 To distance-sq-2d gives the squared Euclidean distance in 2D.
 To distance-sq-3d gives the squared Euclidean distance in 3D.
 To manhattan-2d gives the Manhattan distance in 2D.
 To manhattan-3d gives the Manhattan distance in 3D.
 To midpoint-x gives the x-coordinate of the midpoint of two points.
 To midpoint-y gives the y-coordinate of the midpoint of two points.

 We say:

Section: Dot Product

  punctual dot-2d : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  dot-2d (ax) (ay) (bx) (by) = ax * bx + ay * by

  punctual dot-3d : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  dot-3d (ax) (ay) (az) (bx) (by) (bz) = ax * bx + ay * by + az * bz

Section: Cross Product

  punctual cross-2d : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  cross-2d (ax) (ay) (bx) (by) = ax * by - ay * bx

  punctual cross-3d-x : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  cross-3d-x (ax) (ay) (az) (bx) (by) (bz) = ay * bz - az * by

  punctual cross-3d-y : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  cross-3d-y (ax) (ay) (az) (bx) (by) (bz) = az * bx - ax * bz

  punctual cross-3d-z : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  cross-3d-z (ax) (ay) (az) (bx) (by) (bz) = ax * by - ay * bx

Section: Distance

  punctual distance-sq-2d : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  distance-sq-2d (x1) (y1) (x2) (y2) =
    let dx = x2 - x1 in let dy = y2 - y1 in dx * dx + dy * dy

  punctual distance-sq-3d : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  distance-sq-3d (x1) (y1) (z1) (x2) (y2) (z2) =
    let dx = x2 - x1 in let dy = y2 - y1 in let dz = z2 - z1 in dx * dx + dy * dy + dz * dz

  punctual manhattan-2d : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  manhattan-2d (x1) (y1) (x2) (y2) = int-abs (x2 - x1) + int-abs (y2 - y1)

  punctual manhattan-3d : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  manhattan-3d (x1) (y1) (z1) (x2) (y2) (z2) = int-abs (x2 - x1) + int-abs (y2 - y1) + int-abs (z2 - z1)

Section: Midpoint

  punctual midpoint-x : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  midpoint-x (x1) (x2) = bit-shru (x1 + x2) 1

  punctual midpoint-y : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  midpoint-y (y1) (y2) = bit-shru (y1 + y2) 1

